roper visibility protection setups.","protected fields balance security and flexibility, keeping visibility locked inside packages except for inheriting children.","A defines private behaviors. C defines public profiles. D reverses proper visibility protection setups.","A defines private behaviors. C defines public profiles. D reverses proper visibility protection setups."]},{"question_text":"What happens if you try to use a local variable inside a method before initializing it?","options":["It uses a default value like 0 or null automatically.","It triggers a compilation error indicating uninitialized use.","It causes a NullPointerException only when executed.","The compiler skips that specific processing statement line."],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["A applies exclusively to class level variables. C and D mistake dynamic runtime exceptions for static compilation failures.","Local execution scopes do not receive default field initializations; the developer must assign values before reading them.","A applies exclusively to class level variables. C and D mistake dynamic runtime exceptions for static compilation failures.","A applies exclusively to class level variables. C and D mistake dynamic runtime exceptions for static compilation failures."]},{"question_text":"What is the fundamental purpose of the throw keyword in Java?","options":["To safely log error messages into disk files.","To explicitly trigger an exception instance to propagate.","To sign and declare exception risk metrics on headers.","To terminate an active looping block control structure."],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["A is a logging task. C describes throws on signatures. D describes structural flow operations like break.","throw triggers exception state processing, interrupting normal execution to route control to matching handlers.","A is a logging task. C describes throws on signatures. D describes structural flow operations like break.","A is a logging tas