ion modifiers, stack frame configurations, or constant structures.","A, C, and D confuse this with synchronization modifiers, stack frame configurations, or constant structures."]},{"question_text":"What happens when an exception is thrown from an active static initializer block?","options":["The class loads successfully but skips static elements.","It triggers an ExceptionInInitializerError at runtime.","The system catches it and completes normal loading steps.","It causes a compile-time invalid syntax failure error."],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["A and C compromise safety guarantees. D is wrong because runtime failures bypass static compilation checks.","Uncaught exceptions inside static initialization blocks prevent class loading and trigger an ExceptionInInitializerError.","A and C compromise safety guarantees. D is wrong because runtime failures bypass static compilation checks.","A and C compromise safety guarantees. D is wrong because runtime failures bypass static compilation checks."]},{"question_text":"Which mechanism allows an object to present multiple functional forms based on context?","options":["Encapsulation","Polymorphism","Data Hiding","Composition"],"correct_option_index":1,"option_explanations":["A and C manage object security boundaries. D describes object assembly structural modeling patterns.","Polymorphism allows a parent interface reference to bind to different concrete object variations at runtime.","A and C manage object security boundaries. D describes object assembly structural modeling patterns.","A and C manage object security boundaries. D describes object assembly structural modeling patterns."]},{"question_text":"Consider the following code. What will be the output?\n\n```java\npublic class ShortCircuit {\r\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\r\n        int x = 10;\r\n        if (x > 5 || ++x > 20) { System.out.println(x); }\r\n    }\r\n}\n```","options":["10","11","20","Compile error"],"correct_option